# Source is source, even when a stray control character says otherwise.
#
# git decides "binary" by sniffing the first 8000 bytes for a NUL. One literal
# NUL inside a string literal — a perfectly reasonable separator for a composite
# map key — is enough, and the consequence is silent and total: `git diff` prints
# "Binary files differ", `--numstat` reports `-`/`-`, and GitHub renders no diff,
# no line anchors and no blame. A module can land with nothing for a reviewer to
# read while every test passes, which is exactly what happened to
# `web-app/src/pages/ide/MetricTree/scenario/propagationTrace.ts`.
#
# Marking source extensions `diff` overrides the sniff, so these files always
# render a textual diff — including across a commit whose parent blob really
# does contain the byte. Prefer the two-character escape sequence in the source
# anyway; this is the backstop that makes the next slip reviewable, not invisible.
*.ts    diff
*.tsx   diff
*.js    diff
*.jsx   diff
*.mjs   diff
*.cjs   diff
*.rs    diff
*.py    diff
*.sh    diff
*.md    diff
*.yml   diff
*.yaml  diff
*.json  diff
*.toml  diff
*.css   diff
*.html  diff
*.sql   diff
